---
import Proto3Layout from '../layouts/Proto3Layout.astro';
---
<Proto3Layout>
  <header class="site-head wrap">
    <a class="wordmark" href="#">get smart ai
      <small>led by Ryan Garver</small>
    </a>
    <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Site">
      <a href="#rates">Services</a>
      <a href="#proof">Work</a>
      <a href="#start">Contact</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="sun-patch" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow" data-hero-in>Get Smart AI · led by <b>Ryan Garver</b> · Boise, Idaho + remote</p>
        <h1 data-hero-in>AI that pays for itself. Here's the math.</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub" data-hero-in>Consulting, automation builds, team training, websites, and ready-made kits for businesses that run without an engineering department.</p>
        <p class="ledger-voice" data-hero-in>Every price on this site is published. Every number is real.</p>
        <div class="cta-row" data-hero-in>
          <a class="btn" href="#start">Start with a diagnostic</a>
          <a class="link-arrow" href="#proof">See the work &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="chip" data-hero-in>
          <span>Hiring for AI enablement?</span>
          <a href="#proof">The work and r&eacute;sum&eacute; are one click away &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section id="rates">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="kicker" data-in>The rate card</p>
        <h2 class="sec-title" data-in>What it costs</h2>
        <p class="sec-intro" data-in>Published rates, the way your accountant would insist on. The line items below are the whole list.</p>

        <div class="ledger" data-in>
          <div class="line-item" style="--li: 0">
            <div class="li-row">
              <span class="li-name">The diagnostic</span>
              <span class="leader" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="li-price"><small>from</small>$750</span>
            </div>
            <p class="li-sub">I find what's slow, write up the fixes, and hand you the quick wins. If the report isn't worth the fee, you don't pay it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="line-item" style="--li: 1">
            <div class="li-row">
              <span class="li-name">Automation builds</span>
              <span class="leader" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="li-price"><small>from</small>$2,000</span>
            </div>
            <p class="li-sub">The follow-up that never goes out. The report that eats your Friday. Built, tested, and handed over with instructions.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="line-item" style="--li: 2">
            <div class="li-row">
              <span class="li-name">Websites</span>
              <span class="leader" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="li-price"><small>from</small>$1,500</span>
            </div>
            <p class="li-sub">A site that does its job, live in two weeks. This one is the sample.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="line-item" style="--li: 3">
            <div class="li-row">
              <span class="li-name">Team training</span>
              <span class="leader" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="li-price"><small>from</small>$900</span>
            </div>
            <p class="li-sub">Your people, your tools, a working session. They leave already using it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="line-item" style="--li: 4">
            <div class="li-row">
              <span class="li-name">The follow-up kit</span>
              <span class="leader" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="li-price">$199</span>
            </div>
            <p class="li-sub">Install it yourself. Scripts, templates, and the setup guide.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="ledger-note" data-in>Retainers exist. They're offered after an engagement, never sold cold.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="proof" id="proof">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="kicker" data-in>The proof</p>
        <h2 class="sec-title" data-in>The numbers behind the claims</h2>
        <p class="sec-intro" data-in>Everything on this page traces back to systems I built and run myself.</p>

        <div class="totals" data-in>
          <div class="total">
            <div class="total-figure" data-count="14851">14,851</div>
            <p class="total-label">job postings scored by one system, end to end</p>
          </div>
          <div class="total">
            <div class="total-figure" data-count="616">616</div>
            <p class="total-label">tests passing in that system's suite</p>
          </div>
          <div class="total">
            <div class="total-figure" data-count="0">0</div>
            <p class="total-label">re-score errors across every audit</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="case-line" data-in>
          <p><strong>Operation Hired.</strong> Designed, built, and operated solo: <span class="num">14,851</span> postings scored at <span class="num">$0</span> per posting.</p>
          <a class="link-arrow" href="#">Read the case study &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="principal">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="kicker" data-in>The principal</p>
        <h2 class="sec-title" data-in>The person behind it</h2>
        <p class="principal-body" data-in>I'm Ryan Garver. I run this practice to keep my AI enablement work current and measurable. When I say a tool pays for itself, it's because I built it, ran it, and kept the receipts. If you're hiring for AI enablement, the same work is on the shelf with the numbers attached.</p>
        <p class="signature" data-in>Ryan Garver · Get Smart AI · Boise, Idaho</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="close-cta" id="start">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="kicker" data-in>The next line item</p>
        <h2 class="sec-title" data-in>Tell me what's slow.</h2>
        <p class="close-sub" data-in>I'll tell you what it costs to fix. An intake form, three fields, no sales call.</p>
        <a class="btn" href="#" data-in>Start the conversation</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div class="wrap foot-row">
      <span>Smart Business AI LLC · Boise, Idaho · &copy; 2026</span>
      <span class="foot-links">
        <a href="#">Privacy</a>
        <a href="#">Terms</a>
        <a href="#">Accessibility</a>
      </span>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <button id="dials-toggle" class="dials-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="dials">Dials</button>
  <div id="dials" class="dials" hidden>
    <h3>Open Book dials</h3>
    <div class="dial">
      <label for="d-pace">Entrance pace <b id="d-pace-v">1.0x</b></label>
      <input id="d-pace" type="range" min="0.4" max="2" step="0.1" value="1" />
    </div>
    <div class="dial">
      <label for="d-stagger">Stagger <b id="d-stagger-v">90ms</b></label>
      <input id="d-stagger" type="range" min="20" max="200" step="10" value="90" />
    </div>
    <div class="dial">
      <label for="d-tally">Tally duration <b id="d-tally-v">900ms</b></label>
      <input id="d-tally" type="range" min="300" max="2000" step="50" value="900" />
    </div>
    <div class="dial">
      <label for="d-drift">Sun drift <b id="d-drift-v">48s</b></label>
      <input id="d-drift" type="range" min="16" max="90" step="2" value="48" />
    </div>
    <button id="d-replay" class="replay">Replay entrance</button>
  </div>
</Proto3Layout>
